<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal Jan-Apr global trade deficit 554 bln esc. [CORRECTED 14:28 GMT]</title>
<headline>Portugal Jan-Apr global trade deficit 554 bln esc. [CORRECTED 14:28 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's global trade deficit rose to 554.0 billion escudos between January and April from 492.1 billion in same period last year, the National Statistics Institute (INE) said.</p>
<p>		   Jan-Apr 97 Jan-Apr 96     Apr '97	 Mar '97</p>
<p>(Corrects month in table from May to Mar).</p>
<p> Overall balance   -554.0   -492.1	   -162.9	 -141.7</p>
<p> Imports	    1,797.3 1,752.3	    478.6	   456.2</p>
<p> Exports	    1,243.3 1,260.2	    315.7	   314.5</p>
<p>Note - Figures are in billions of escudos. A minus sign denotes a deficit.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
